# Markdown ~80-character lines

When creating or editing Markdown in this repo, wrap prose to about
80 characters per line (same convention as CallerTips).

- Prefer soft wraps at word boundaries near column 80.
- A few characters over is fine; do not obsess over exact width.
- Do not rewrap untouched paragraphs when making unrelated edits.
- Leave these unwrapped when wrapping would hurt readability:
  - long URLs and markdown links with long targets
  - tables
  - image / HTML embed lines
  - fenced code blocks
  - headings (unless a heading is unusually long)

Match the surrounding file's wrap style when editing existing prose.
